This approach enables the model to answer questions using both retrieved context and transformer-based reasoning.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Knowledge Base Creation\n\nIn Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), the first step is to construct a knowledge base containing the correct answers from the training dataset. Each correct answer serves as a document that can later be retrieved using semantic similarity search.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"kb = []\n\nfor _, row in train_df.iterrows():\n    correct_letter = row[\"answer\"]\n    kb.append(str(row[correct_letter]))\n\nprint(f\"Knowledge base created with {len(kb)} documents.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.162320Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.162619Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.242218Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.162592Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.241489Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Knowledge base created with 1600 documents.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":33},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Building the FAISS Index\n\nThe knowledge base documents are converted into dense vector embeddings using the Sentence Transformer model. These embeddings are then indexed using FAISS, enabling efficient similarity search during retrieval.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"kb_embeddings = embedding_model.encode(\n    kb,\n    convert_to_numpy=True,\n    show_progress_bar=True\n)\n\n\nindex = faiss.IndexFlatL2(kb_embeddings.shape[1])\nindex.add(kb_embeddings)\n\nprint(f\"Indexed {index.ntotal} documents.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.243184Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.243481Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.123684Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-30T16:21:59.243459Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.122949Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Batches:   0%|          | 0/50 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"5a5709c0fef84f279e9bc8c41754439d"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Indexed 1600 documents.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":34},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Dense Retrieval using FAISS\n\nGiven a question, we first generate its embedding using the Sentence Transformer model. The embedding is then used to query the FAISS index, retrieving the top-k most semantically similar documents from the knowledge base. These retrieved documents serve as candidate contexts for the subsequent reranking stage.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def retrieve_documents(prompt, k=5):\n    \"\"\"\n    Retrieve the top-k most similar documents from the knowledge base.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    prompt_embedding = embedding_model.encode(\n        [prompt],\n        convert_to_numpy=True\n    )\n\n    distances, indices = index.search(prompt_embedding, k)\n\n    retrieved_docs = [kb[i] for i in indices[0]]\n\n    return retrieved_docs, indices[0], distances[0]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.124535Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.125013Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.129840Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.124989Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.129099Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":35},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cross-Encoder Reranking\n\nThe initial retrieval step uses a bi-encoder, which retrieves documents efficiently based on embedding similarity. However, embedding similarity alone may not capture the exact semantic relationship between the question and the retrieved document.\n\nTo improve retrieval quality, we use a Cross-Encoder. Unlike a bi-encoder, the Cross-Encoder processes the question and each retrieved document together, allowing the attention mechanism to directly model interactions between them. The retrieved documents are then reranked based on their semantic relevance scores.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"cross_encoder = CrossEncoder(\n    \"cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2\"\n)\n\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.130752Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.131063Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-30T16:22:03.227654Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-30T16:22:00.131026Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-30T16:22:03.226621Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"config.json:   0%|          | 0.00/794 [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"4e881efcb5d74972b03968fab181ad2c"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"model.safetensors:   0%|          | 0.00/90.9M [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"86b26b52232e47b3a24949a729161089"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/105 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"5f86d724ec014058aaa9caf81a4477e4"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stderr","text":"BertForSequenceClassification LOAD REPORT from: cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2\nKey                          | Status     |  | \n-----------------------------+------------+--+-\nbert.embeddings.position_ids | UNEXPECTED |  | \n\nNotes:\n- UNEXPECTED\t:can be ignored when loading from different task/architecture; not ok if you expect identical arch.\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"tokenizer_config.json: 0.00B [00:00, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"9e76c2633fe24beab5c2ce5b90cdb3a8"}},"metadata"